    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on speed and favorable matchups, headlined by **Trea Turner** (81.27) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98). **Trea Turner** remains our premier start, leveraging a soft matchup against the left-handed Andrew Abbott, with his elite sprint speed bolstered by a +19% SP skill adjustment. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is equally compelling despite a 33% rain risk; his score is inflated by a massive +16% park factor and the presence of a slow-delivery pitcher that creates an optimal environment for his stolen base upside. **Kyle Schwarber** (79.42) rounds out our top-tier trio, benefiting from the same favorable matchup against Abbott to drive a high-ceiling performance.\n\nMid-tier value is anchored by **Colt Keith** (63.93) and **Junior Caminero** (60.79), both of whom capitalize on positive platoon dynamics and advantageous spots in the order. While **Yordan Alvarez** (49.70) remains a force with a 0.479 xwOBA, his score is suppressed today by a challenging matchup against an elite arm (3.11 xERA) and an unfavorable platoon split. The most difficult decision rested on the bench, where **Josh Smith** (49.83) narrowly missed the final lineup spot. While **Josh Smith** offers a solid base floor and potential for situational steals, the optimizer opted for the higher aggregate daily efficiency of **Carson Benge** (58.92), who projects better against the current pitching environment. We will continue to monitor the weather in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s game, as any rain-induced delay could force a late pivot to our bench assets.",
